<section class="philosophy">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-label">ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY</h2>
    <p class="philosophy-intro">
      How problems are approached.
    </p>

    <div class="philosophy-steps">
      <div class="philosophy-step">
        <span class="step-marker">01</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-title">Understand</h3>
          <p class="step-description">
            Define the actual problem, not the symptoms. Identify constraints,
            failure modes, and real user needs before touching architecture.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-step">
        <span class="step-marker">02</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-title">Structure</h3>
          <p class="step-description">
            Design the system boundaries, data flow, and component responsibilities
            before implementation. Structure determines scalability and maintainability.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-step">
        <span class="step-marker">03</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-title">Automate</h3>
          <p class="step-description">
            Eliminate repetition. Every manual step is a failure point waiting to
            happen. Build resilience into the automation, not around it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-step">
        <span class="step-marker">04</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-title">Deliver</h3>
          <p class="step-description">
            Ship working software with evidence, documentation, and clear ownership.
            An unmaintained system is a system that will eventually fail.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

